---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Collibra Product Innovations case study | Kyle Murray"
  description="How Kyle Murray authored and coordinated a Collibra product innovations page in Sanity, aligned its presentation to Figma, and validated content, links, imagery, and release dates."
>
<main class="web-ops-page">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Professional work · Web production and launch coordination</p>
    <h1>Making product innovations easier to navigate.</h1>
    <p class="lede">At Collibra, I handled Sanity authoring, component presentation, metadata, internal links, QA, and launch coordination for a product innovations page that helped visitors distinguish what was new from what was coming next.</p>
    <p><strong>Tools and inputs:</strong> Sanity, Figma designs, stakeholder copy and imagery, and a launch QA checklist.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ops-section">
    <h2>The delivery challenge</h2>
    <p>The page needed to bring product updates together with clear timelines and accurate dates. Delivering that experience involved both assembling the content in Sanity and getting the components to display correctly against the Figma designs.</p>
    <p>Content readiness was another dependency: copy and assets arrived at different times from stakeholders. Coordinating those inputs was part of the work required to bring the page to launch.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ops-section">
    <h2>My contribution</h2>
    <div class="ops-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>CMS authoring and components</h3>
        <p>I authored the page in Sanity and worked through component adjustments to align the presentation with the Figma reference.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Metadata and internal links</h3>
        <p>I handled page metadata and internal linking, and checked that links led to the intended destinations.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Content and launch coordination</h3>
        <p>I coordinated the copy and content needed from stakeholders and the work required to launch the page.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Quality assurance</h3>
        <p>I used a checklist to review links, spacing, imagery against Figma, navigation, and the footer.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p>The visual design was supplied through Figma, and stakeholders supplied the product content. My role focused on bringing those inputs into the CMS, validating the implementation, and coordinating launch.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ops-section">
    <h2>Working through the details</h2>
    <p>Component presentation took iteration to match the design. Spacing and image alignment needed attention alongside the copy itself; having content entered in the CMS did not mean the page was ready to publish.</p>
    <p>The content dependencies also meant that production and coordination went together. I needed the necessary copy and assets from stakeholders to complete the page, while keeping the new and upcoming innovation content clear and correctly dated.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ops-section">
    <h2>What I checked</h2>
    <p>This is a retrospective summary of the checks I remember using, not a reproduction of an internal Collibra document.</p>
    <div class="ops-table-wrap">
      <table class="ops-table">
        <caption>QA areas and review focus</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Review focus</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Links</th><td>Correct destinations, including internal links.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Component presentation</th><td>Spacing and layout against the Figma reference.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Images</th><td>Alignment and presentation against the supplied design.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Page context</th><td>Navigation and footer included in the review.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Innovation content</th><td>Correct publication dates for new and upcoming items.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ops-section">
    <h2>The delivered result</h2>
    <p>The version I authored brought new and upcoming innovations into a clearer timeline experience, with a timeline feature on the left, cleaner imagery, and correct publication dates for both categories.</p>
    <p>From my production perspective, visitors had a clearer way to access what was new and what was upcoming. This is a qualitative account of the delivered experience; I do not have analytics or usability-test results to quantify the improvement.</p>
    <p>The work demonstrates my ability to take supplied designs and product content through CMS authoring, component refinement, QA, and launch coordination.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ops-section" aria-labelledby="project-graphics-title">
    <h2 id="project-graphics-title">Selected graphics from the project</h2>
    <p>These original product graphics are retained from the Product Innovations project. They illustrate the visual material involved in the page work; they are not screenshots of the finished page or evidence of its timeline layout.</p>
    <p><strong>Artwork credit:</strong> Collibra. My contribution was CMS authoring, component presentation, QA, and launch coordination.</p>

    <figure class="project-graphic">
      <a href="/images/case-studies/collibra/semantic-mapping.png" aria-label="Open semantic mapping graphic at full size">
        <img src="/images/case-studies/collibra/semantic-mapping.png" width="1440" height="810" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Collibra product illustration combining a Stewardship interface with Generate new model and Automated Stitching panels." />
      </a>
      <figcaption><strong>Semantic mapping and model generation.</strong> A detailed interface illustration combining several panels. It provides context for the imagery and design-alignment work described in this case study. <a href="/images/case-studies/collibra/semantic-mapping.png">View full-size graphic →</a></figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="project-graphic">
      <a href="/images/case-studies/collibra/data-lineage.png" aria-label="Open data lineage graphic at full size">
        <img src="/images/case-studies/collibra/data-lineage.png" width="1440" height="810" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Citizen Benefits technical lineage illustration connecting application and caseworker systems through eligibility checks to notification, disbursement, and open-data outputs." />
      </a>
      <figcaption><strong>Technical lineage for self-hosted deployments.</strong> A product graphic using a citizen-benefits example to show relationships between systems. <a href="/images/case-studies/collibra/data-lineage.png">View full-size graphic →</a></figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="project-graphic">
      <a href="/images/case-studies/collibra/mcp-server.png" aria-label="Open MCP server graphic at full size">
        <img src="/images/case-studies/collibra/mcp-server.png" width="1440" height="810" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Product diagram showing MCP clients connected through a consumer and MCP server to Business Glossary, Asset Recommender, and future tools." />
      </a>
      <figcaption><strong>MCP server.</strong> A conceptual product illustration connecting AI clients with Collibra tools. <a href="/images/case-studies/collibra/mcp-server.png">View full-size graphic →</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="ops-section">
    <h2>About the live reference</h2>
    <p>Collibra has redesigned this page since the version I authored. The current page is linked for project context; its present styling and later updates should not be attributed to me.</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.collibra.com/products/innovations">View Collibra’s current Product Innovations page →</a></p>
    <p>This case study is based on my recollection of the work. The selected graphics above are original project assets. Screenshots of my finished page and the original QA checklist are not included.</p>
  </section>
  <p><a href="/projects">Back to projects →</a> · <a href="/contact">Discuss my web production work →</a></p>
</main>
</BaseLayout>

